# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.25.1
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-BRACES-19963945:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          braces has no fixed version: 3.0.3 is the latest published release and every version is
          affected (CVE-2026-93687). It reaches this project only through Sanity's CLI tooling
          (micromatch, chokidar and fast-glob below @sanity/cli and @sanity/codegen), which expands
          glob patterns from this repository's own configuration and never outside input. Revisit
          once braces publishes a patched release.
        expires: 2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-DEEPMERGE-19964053:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          deepmerge has no fixed version: 4.3.1 is the latest published release and every version
          from 4.2.0 is affected (CVE-2026-93753). It reaches this project only through
          html-to-text below @react-email/render, which merges its own options with its defaults;
          the rendered mail content never passes through the merge. Revisit once deepmerge
          publishes a patched release.
        expires: 2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-ZOD-20510278:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          zod 4.6.6 fixes CVE-2023-54404, and the web app runs 4.6.7. The remaining match is zod
          3.25.76, which reaches this project only through chromium-bidi below @lhci/cli
          (lighthouse, puppeteer-core), a dev dependency that parses the DevTools protocol messages
          of a local Chrome during a Lighthouse run and never outside input. The 3.x line has no
          fixed release. Revisit once chromium-bidi moves to zod 4.
        expires: 2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z
patch: {}
